# UPGRADE-18
# Local AI Quality Engineering & Continuous Optimization
#
# Project-Specific Quality Benchmarks
# Model / Prompt / Tool Profile Evaluation
# Automatic Promotion & Quarantine
# Regression Detection
# A/B / Canary Routing
# Continuous No-Cost Optimization
#
# PRIMARY PRINCIPLES:
#
# NO-COST FIRST
# LOCAL-FIRST
# QUALITY > RAW TOKENS/SECOND
# TEST RESULTS > MODEL SELF-RATING
# NO SILENT PAID FALLBACK
# NO HIDDEN QUALITY FABRICATION
# NO CUSTOMER CODE UPLOAD
# NO CHAIN-OF-THOUGHT STORAGE

You are operating directly inside ZCoder after Upgrade-17.

================================================================
MISSION
================================================================

Upgrade-17 reportedly introduced:

- runtime supervision
- model pool
- hot/warm/cold residency
- memory admission
- inference scheduler
- backpressure
- zero-paid-call enforcement

Upgrade-18 must answer a different question:

"Which local model + runtime configuration + prompt/tool profile
actually produces the best engineering outcome for THIS project?"

The system must evolve from:

model routing based primarily on
capability/performance/hardware

to:

routing based on
capability
+
measured coding correctness
+
project compatibility
+
tool reliability
+
validation history
+
latency
+
memory
+
cost policy

Target architecture:

Project
   │
   ▼
Quality Profile
   │
   ├── benchmark fixtures
   ├── validators
   ├── language/framework
   ├── tool requirements
   └── quality thresholds
   │
   ▼
Evaluation Engine
   │
   ├── Model A + Prompt Profile 1
   ├── Model A + Prompt Profile 2
   ├── Model B + Prompt Profile 1
   └── ...
   │
   ▼
Measured Outcomes
   │
   ├── tests passed
   ├── regressions
   ├── patch quality
   ├── tool correctness
   ├── attempts
   ├── latency
   └── resource usage
   │
   ▼
Promotion Engine
   │
   ├── PREFERRED
   ├── CANDIDATE
   ├── DEGRADED
   ├── QUARANTINED
   └── RETIRED
   │
   ▼
Adaptive Router

================================================================
PHASE 0 — FORENSICALLY VERIFY UPGRADE-17
================================================================

Run:

git status --short
git log -30 --oneline
git tag --sort=-version:refname | head -30

python -m pytest -q -ra
python main.py --version
python -m build
git diff --check

Run release gate.

Inspect:

local_ai_stack.py
agent_runtime.py
no_cost_platform.py
release_gate.py
runtime supervisor
model pool
scheduler
benchmark/performance modules
tests/

Produce:

UPGRADE-17 EVIDENCE MATRIX

Capability
Claimed Tier
Actual Evidence
Real Runtime?
Real Model?
Correct Tier
Verdict

Do not elevate evidence from prose.

================================================================
1. E4 REALITY RULE
================================================================

LOCAL_RUNTIME_VERIFIED may be E4 only when evidence contains:

actual model artifact
actual digest
actual runtime
actual generated tokens
actual network/runtime request
actual response
actual timing

LOCAL_CODING_VERIFIED may be E4 only when:

actual model
actual repository fixture
actual patch
actual test execution
actual successful repair

If not present:

keep E2/E3.

================================================================
2. QUALITY ENGINEERING DOMAIN
================================================================

Create:

QualityEngineeringService

Responsibilities:

benchmark definitions
evaluation execution
scoring
baselines
regression detection
promotion
quarantine
canary analysis
routing evidence

Do not put these responsibilities directly inside LocalInferenceScheduler.

================================================================
3. QUALITY PROFILE
================================================================

Create:

QualityProfile

Fields conceptually:

id
name
project_id
language
framework
task_classes
required_validators
required_tools
minimum_quality
maximum_attempts
benchmark_suite
version

================================================================
4. PROJECT-SPECIFIC QUALITY
================================================================

A model good for generic Python must not automatically become preferred
for:

React
Rust
Go
Terraform
PowerShell

without evidence.

Allow project-specific evidence.

================================================================
5. TASK CLASSIFICATION
================================================================

Start with deterministic task classes:

CODE_REPAIR
CODE_GENERATION
REFACTOR
TEST_GENERATION
CODE_REVIEW
DOCUMENTATION
SECURITY_REVIEW
STRUCTURED_TOOL_TASK
RAG_CODE_SEARCH

Do not use another paid LLM simply to classify task.

================================================================
6. TASK REQUIREMENTS
================================================================

Each class defines requirements.

Example:

CODE_REPAIR:
    code=true
    repository_tools=true
    tests=true

STRUCTURED_TOOL_TASK:
    tools=true
    structured_output=true

================================================================
7. QUALITY BENCHMARK SUITE
================================================================

Create:

QualityBenchmarkSuite

Contain deterministic small fixtures.

Do not depend on customer repository for default product benchmarks.

================================================================
8. BENCHMARK FIXTURE
================================================================

Fixture contains:

repository
initial commit/hash
task
expected invariants
validators
time/token limits
allowed files
forbidden changes

================================================================
9. FIXTURE VERSION
================================================================

Every fixture must be versioned.

Changing expected test or repository content:

new benchmark version.

================================================================
10. CODE REPAIR FIXTURES
================================================================

Create representative fixtures.

Examples:

Python bug
TypeScript bug
configuration error
small refactor

Keep them small enough for CPU local models.

================================================================
11. REAL VALIDATION
================================================================

Quality score comes from:

pytest
unit tests
lint
typecheck
build
project validator

not:

"model says task completed."

================================================================
12. TESTS BEFORE / AFTER
================================================================

Record:

baseline failing tests
post-patch passing tests
new regressions

A benchmark cannot score success if tests were already passing before.

================================================================
13. PATCH VALIDITY
================================================================

Measure:

patch applies
syntax valid
scope allowed
forbidden files untouched
validation passes

================================================================
14. DIFF SIZE
================================================================

Record:

files changed
lines added
lines deleted

Do not automatically prefer smaller patch if larger change is actually
required.

================================================================
15. UNRELATED CHANGE PENALTY
================================================================

Benchmark may penalize:

unnecessary unrelated modifications
configuration drift
generated junk
dependency changes not required

================================================================
16. SECURITY PENALTY
================================================================

Automatic failure/strong penalty for:

secret exposure
disabled security check
unsafe shell behavior
test deletion
validation bypass

================================================================
17. TEST DELETION DEFENSE
================================================================

A model must not "solve" benchmark by deleting or weakening tests.

Detect:

test removal
skip injection
assert removal
validator bypass

================================================================
18. QUALITY RESULT
================================================================

Create:

QualityResult

Fields:

model
digest
runtime
runtime profile
prompt profile
tool profile
benchmark
attempt

validation_result
correctness
regression_count
tool_accuracy
patch_scope
latency
resource_usage

status

================================================================
19. QUALITY STATUS
================================================================

Use:

PASS
PARTIAL
FAIL
TIMEOUT
RUNTIME_ERROR
POLICY_DENIED

================================================================
20. DO NOT COLLAPSE FAILURE TYPES
================================================================

Model quality failure != runtime failure.

Examples:

model produced wrong patch
→ QUALITY_FAIL

server crashed
→ RUNTIME_FAIL

tool denied by policy
→ POLICY_FAIL

================================================================
21. QUALITY SCORE
================================================================

Use objective weighted components.

For coding repair:

correctness dominates.

Example conceptual weighting:

validation correctness: 60%
regression safety: 20%
tool reliability: 10%
patch discipline: 10%

Performance is considered separately.

Do not let 2x faster model beat a model that actually fixes code.

================================================================
22. PERFORMANCE SCORE SEPARATION
================================================================

Keep:

QUALITY_SCORE

and:

PERFORMANCE_SCORE

separate.

Router may combine them according to task preference.

================================================================
23. COMPOSITE ROUTING SCORE
================================================================

Composite routing may consider:

quality
performance
availability
memory
warmth
cost
residency

But quality floor is mandatory.

================================================================
24. QUALITY FLOOR
================================================================

Example:

minimum_quality = 0.80

Candidate below floor:

ineligible

even if fastest.

================================================================
25. FIRST-PASS SUCCESS
================================================================

Measure:

first-pass success rate

separately from:

eventual success after repair loop.

================================================================
26. ATTEMPT EFFICIENCY
================================================================

Record number of:

model turns
tool calls
repair cycles

A model requiring 12 retries is meaningfully different from first-pass
success.

================================================================
27. TOOL RELIABILITY
================================================================

Measure:

correct tool selection
valid schema
valid arguments
policy compliance
result handling

Across repeated fixtures.

================================================================
28. TOOL HALLUCINATION
================================================================

Record attempted call to nonexistent tool.

Do not silently convert it into success.

================================================================
29. TOOL PROFILE
================================================================

Create:

ToolProfile

Example:

minimal_coding
full_repository
review_only

Do not expose every tool to every local model by default.

================================================================
30. PROMPT PROFILE
================================================================

Create versioned:

PromptProfile

Contains:

system/template
task formatting
context strategy
tool instructions
output contract

Do not store private chain-of-thought.

================================================================
31. PROMPT PROFILE VERSIONING
================================================================

A prompt change creates new version/hash.

Historical results remain attributable.

================================================================
32. PROMPT OPTIMIZER
================================================================

Create deterministic bounded evaluator:

same model
same benchmark
different prompt profile

Compare outcomes.

Do not use paid LLM to rewrite prompts automatically in core mode.

================================================================
33. PROMPT CANDIDATES
================================================================

Start from manually-defined/template-generated variants.

Examples:

compact
tool-explicit
test-first
plan-before-edit

================================================================
34. PROMPT OPTIMIZATION SAFETY
================================================================

Never optimize system prompt by weakening:

policy
security
approval
tenant boundary
paid-provider firewall

Immutable security instruction layer remains outside optimized profile.

================================================================
35. TOOL-PROMPT COOPTIMIZATION
================================================================

Model quality may depend on:

prompt
tool description
schema

Measure combinations where useful.

================================================================
36. TOOL SCHEMA VERSIONING
================================================================

Changing schema invalidates relevant benchmark evidence.

================================================================
37. CONTEXT PROFILE
================================================================

Create:

ContextProfile

Possible strategies:

RAG_ONLY
RAG_PLUS_KEY_FILES
RECENT_TOOL_CONTEXT
LARGER_CONTEXT

================================================================
38. CONTEXT QUALITY BENCHMARK
================================================================

Compare retrieval/context strategies.

Do not assume maximum context produces best result.

================================================================
39. RAG EVALUATION
================================================================

Measure:

relevant file retrieval
irrelevant context
missing target symbol

Separate retrieval error from model reasoning failure.

================================================================
40. PROJECT BENCHMARK
================================================================

Allow project to define safe benchmark command.

Example:

pytest tests/smoke
npm test -- ...
go test ./...

Project benchmark runs sandboxed according to existing tool policy.

================================================================
41. PROJECT BENCHMARK SAFETY
================================================================

Never automatically run arbitrary repository benchmark configuration
from untrusted PR without policy/approval.

================================================================
42. PROJECT QUALITY BASELINE
================================================================

Store:

preferred model
quality profile
prompt profile
runtime profile
last verified commit/config
quality result
performance result

================================================================
43. MODEL PROMOTION STATES
================================================================

Separate artifact state from quality state.

Quality lifecycle:

UNTESTED
CANDIDATE
VALIDATED
PREFERRED
DEGRADED
QUARANTINED
RETIRED

================================================================
44. PROMOTION ENGINE
================================================================

Create:

ModelPromotionService

Model becomes PREFERRED only after satisfying configured evidence.

================================================================
45. PROMOTION REQUIREMENTS
================================================================

Example:

minimum sample count
quality floor
no security failure
no critical regression
compatible hardware
zero-cost policy

================================================================
46. NO ONE-SAMPLE PROMOTION
================================================================

One successful task is insufficient for HIGH-confidence global
promotion.

================================================================
47. PROJECT PROMOTION
================================================================

A model may be:

PREFERRED for Project A

and:

CANDIDATE for Project B.

================================================================
48. GLOBAL DEFAULT
================================================================

Global preference requires broader evidence.

Do not derive global default from one repository.

================================================================
49. QUARANTINE
================================================================

Model/profile becomes QUARANTINED on:

critical security violation
repeated invalid tools
major quality regression
repeated runtime crash
corrupt artifact

================================================================
50. QUARANTINE SCOPE
================================================================

Quarantine may apply to:

artifact
runtime profile
prompt profile
model-project combination

Do not over-quarantine unrelated configuration.

================================================================
51. AUTOMATIC QUARANTINE
================================================================

Critical deterministic security failure may automatically quarantine.

Quality-only decline should follow configurable threshold.

================================================================
52. QUARANTINE AUDIT
================================================================

Record:

reason
evidence
timestamp
actor/system
scope

================================================================
53. RELEASE FROM QUARANTINE
================================================================

Require revalidation.

Do not simply flip boolean.

================================================================
54. LAST KNOWN GOOD
================================================================

Keep last-known-good:

model
runtime
prompt
tool
quality evidence

================================================================
55. SAFE ROLLBACK
================================================================

If newly promoted profile regresses:

rollback to last known good.

================================================================
56. MODEL UPDATE PIPELINE
================================================================

New model digest:

CANDIDATE
→ benchmark
→ quality suite
→ canary
→ promote

Never:

latest tag
→ PREFERRED automatically.

================================================================
57. RUNTIME UPDATE PIPELINE
================================================================

New llama.cpp/Ollama/vLLM version:

re-run:

runtime contract
quality smoke
performance smoke

before normal promotion.

================================================================
58. PROMPT UPDATE PIPELINE
================================================================

Prompt change:

candidate
→ benchmark
→ compare
→ canary
→ promote

================================================================
59. TOOL CHANGE PIPELINE
================================================================

Tool/schema changes may invalidate quality profiles.

Revalidation required.

================================================================
60. QUALITY REGRESSION
================================================================

Create:

QualityRegressionDetector

Compare candidate against baseline.

================================================================
61. REGRESSION TYPES
================================================================

Track:

correctness regression
tool regression
security regression
latency regression
memory regression

Separate severity.

================================================================
62. QUALITY THRESHOLDS
================================================================

Example:

first-pass success -20%
tool success -15%
critical security failure >=1

Use configurable policy.

================================================================
63. ABSOLUTE VS RELATIVE
================================================================

Small sample sizes require caution.

Do not declare regression from trivial random variance.

================================================================
64. BENCHMARK SAMPLE SIZE
================================================================

Persist sample count.

Confidence should reflect evidence volume.

================================================================
65. CONFIDENCE MODEL
================================================================

Possible:

LOW
MEDIUM
HIGH

Inputs:

real vs simulated
same project?
same hardware?
sample count
recency
benchmark version

================================================================
66. EVIDENCE DECAY
================================================================

Old benchmark evidence becomes stale when:

model changed
runtime changed
hardware changed
project changed materially
prompt changed
tool schema changed

================================================================
67. EVIDENCE FRESHNESS
================================================================

Persist:

fresh
stale
invalidated

Do not delete historical evidence.

================================================================
68. PROJECT CHANGE FINGERPRINT
================================================================

Quality baseline may include:

language/framework fingerprint
dependency lock hashes
key config hash

Do not invalidate everything for README edit.

================================================================
69. CANARY ROUTING
================================================================

Introduce optional local canary.

Example:

90% preferred
10% candidate

Only for jobs safe for evaluation.

================================================================
70. CANARY MUST NOT DOUBLE EXECUTE
================================================================

Do not run two models that both mutate same working branch.

Use:

shadow evaluation
isolated fixture
or non-mutating comparison

for unsafe tasks.

================================================================
71. SHADOW EVALUATION
================================================================

Candidate may process copied context without committing mutation.

Never expose candidate result as authoritative unless selected.

================================================================
72. A/B ROUTING
================================================================

Use A/B only where:

tenant policy permits
task is comparable
security is maintained

No external analytics required.

================================================================
73. DETERMINISTIC ASSIGNMENT
================================================================

Where A/B is used:

stable hash assignment

rather than random every retry.

================================================================
74. A/B METRICS
================================================================

Compare:

success
first-pass
attempts
latency
tool accuracy
validation

not user "likes" alone.

================================================================
75. BANDIT ROUTING
================================================================

Optional future optimization.

Do NOT introduce complex reinforcement/bandit algorithm unless simple
A/B evidence demonstrates need.

Upgrade-18 should stay understandable.

================================================================
76. ADAPTIVE ROUTER V2
================================================================

Router inputs:

task
project
required capabilities
quality floor
quality evidence
performance evidence
runtime health
warmth
memory
cost
residency

================================================================
77. ROUTING ORDER
================================================================

Mandatory constraints first:

security
authorization
cost
residency
capabilities

Then:

quality

Then optimization:

latency
warmth
memory/load

================================================================
78. NO QUALITY EVIDENCE
================================================================

If model has no project-specific quality evidence:

use broader compatible evidence

and lower confidence.

================================================================
79. QUALITY OVERRIDES PERFORMANCE
================================================================

A candidate below quality floor cannot be selected merely because hot.

================================================================
80. ROUTING EXPLANATION
================================================================

Persist explanation:

selected model
quality
confidence
benchmark
runtime state
cost
rejected candidates

No hidden chain-of-thought.

================================================================
81. MANUAL MODEL PIN
================================================================

Operator may pin model.

Still enforce:

security
cost
fit

Warn if quality evidence is poor/stale.

================================================================
82. QUALITY-BASED FALLBACK
================================================================

Preferred model produces repeated invalid output:

bounded retry

then another eligible local model if policy permits.

Never paid fallback under zero-cost profile.

================================================================
83. FAILURE FINGERPRINT
================================================================

Classify repeated failures.

Example:

INVALID_TOOL_SCHEMA
TEST_FAILURE
JSON_FAILURE
TIMEOUT
MODEL_REFUSAL

Use for fallback decisions.

================================================================
84. NO-PROGRESS DETECTOR
================================================================

Detect repeating identical edits/tool failures.

Stop bounded loop.

Do not burn CPU forever.

================================================================
85. SELF-CRITIQUE BOUNDARY
================================================================

Model may review its output, but this is not independent quality
evidence.

External validators remain authoritative.

================================================================
86. INDEPENDENT LOCAL REVIEWER
================================================================

Optional second local model for review if hardware/cost policy permits.

Do not require multi-model review on constrained host.

================================================================
87. REVIEWER VALUE TEST
================================================================

Measure whether local reviewer improves final validation.

Do not assume another LLM automatically increases quality.

================================================================
88. CONTINUOUS QUALITY JOB
================================================================

Create low-frequency maintenance job.

Triggers:

new model
new model digest
new runtime
new prompt profile
new tool schema
manual request

================================================================
89. DO NOT CONTINUOUSLY BURN CPU
================================================================

Quality benchmarking must not run constantly.

Require idle/maintenance policy.

================================================================
90. HOST IDLE CHECK
================================================================

Optional benchmark scheduling considers:

active developer jobs
CPU load
memory pressure

================================================================
91. BENCHMARK BUDGET
================================================================

Even zero-cost compute has resource cost.

Allow:

max benchmark runtime
max CPU
max model turns

================================================================
92. QUALITY DATABASE
================================================================

Persist normalized:

benchmark suites
runs
results
baselines
promotions
quarantines
regressions

Use existing local DB/storage abstraction.

No external database required.

================================================================
93. SQLITE
================================================================

CORE_FREE supports SQLite.

================================================================
94. POSTGRESQL
================================================================

Self-hosted multi-process can use PostgreSQL.

Tenant isolation must remain.

================================================================
95. TENANT-SCOPED QUALITY DATA
================================================================

Project/customer benchmark data must be tenant scoped.

No quality result leakage across tenant private projects.

================================================================
96. GLOBAL FIXTURE DATA
================================================================

Built-in public synthetic fixtures may be global/shared.

Keep distinct from private project evidence.

================================================================
97. PRIVATE CODE STORAGE
================================================================

Do not store entire repository content in benchmark records.

Store:

hashes
metrics
patch metadata
bounded diagnostics

unless existing secure artifact policy explicitly stores fixture.

================================================================
98. CHAIN OF THOUGHT
================================================================

Never store hidden reasoning.

Quality system may store:

final answer
tool calls
patch
validators
metrics

not private chain-of-thought.

================================================================
99. PROMPT PRIVACY
================================================================

Project prompt content remains local.

No remote optimization service.

================================================================
100. LOCAL ANALYTICS
================================================================

Quality dashboards use local analytics.

No PostHog/Mixpanel dependency.

================================================================
101. QUALITY DASHBOARD
================================================================

Add self-hosted view:

Preferred Models
Candidates
Quality Scores
Performance
Regressions
Quarantine
Prompt Profiles
Project Baselines

No fake metrics.

================================================================
102. QUALITY HISTORY
================================================================

Show timeline:

model digest
runtime version
quality
promotion/quarantine

================================================================
103. MATRIX VIEW
================================================================

Useful view:

           Python Project A   TS Project B
Model X       92%               61%
Model Y       84%               89%

Evidence counts and freshness required.

================================================================
104. PROMPT PROFILE UI
================================================================

Allow authorized users to:

view
clone
edit candidate
benchmark
promote

Never directly edit immutable historical version.

================================================================
105. PROMOTION UX
================================================================

Show:

candidate vs baseline
quality
latency
memory
sample count
regressions

before manual promotion.

================================================================
106. QUARANTINE UX
================================================================

Show clear reason.

Allow:

re-test
retire
remove quarantine after validation

================================================================
107. CLI
================================================================

Target commands:

zcoder quality status

zcoder quality benchmarks
zcoder quality run --project ...
zcoder quality compare ...

zcoder quality baselines
zcoder quality regressions

zcoder models promote MODEL
zcoder models quarantine MODEL
zcoder models validate MODEL

zcoder prompts list
zcoder prompts benchmark PROFILE

================================================================
108. QUALITY EXPLAIN
================================================================

Provide:

zcoder quality explain --project P --task coding

Return:

selected configuration
quality evidence
confidence
freshness
performance
reason

================================================================
109. PROJECT INIT
================================================================

When onboarding project:

detect language/framework
recommend initial quality profile

Do not run expensive benchmark automatically.

================================================================
110. BUILT-IN QUALITY PROFILES
================================================================

Examples:

python
typescript
go
rust
generic

Keep validators configurable.

================================================================
111. LANGUAGE DETECTION
================================================================

Use deterministic repository signals:

file extensions
manifest files
build files

No LLM needed.

================================================================
112. PYTHON PROFILE
================================================================

Potential validators:

pytest
ruff
mypy

only when project actually configures/contains them.

Do not require every tool.

================================================================
113. NODE PROFILE
================================================================

Discover:

package manager
test
lint
typecheck

from project metadata.

Do not invent commands.

================================================================
114. VALIDATOR DISCOVERY
================================================================

Reuse existing project validation discovery.

Never execute arbitrary untrusted configuration without sandbox/policy.

================================================================
115. QUALITY E2E
================================================================

Required deterministic E2E:

two FakeLocalModels:

Model A:
fast
wrong patch

Model B:
slower
correct patch

Router must select B after quality evidence exists.

================================================================
116. PROMOTION E2E
================================================================

Candidate beats baseline on required quality suite.

Promote.

Subsequent routing uses candidate.

================================================================
117. QUARANTINE E2E
================================================================

Candidate triggers security/critical regression.

Automatically quarantine.

Router stops selecting it.

================================================================
118. ROLLBACK E2E
================================================================

Promoted model later regresses.

Return to last known good.

================================================================
119. PROMPT A/B E2E
================================================================

Same model.

Profile A fails tools.
Profile B passes.

Promote B.

================================================================
120. QUALITY EVIDENCE INVALIDATION E2E
================================================================

Change model digest.

Old baseline becomes stale.

Router lowers confidence.

================================================================
121. REAL MODEL QUALITY TEST
================================================================

If real local runtime/model exists:

execute real coding fixtures.

Report separately.

Do not substitute FakeLocalModel.

================================================================
122. REAL MODEL SAMPLE COUNT
================================================================

Do not claim broad coding quality based on one fixture.

Report actual number.

================================================================
123. PROJECT REAL BENCHMARK
================================================================

Optional manual:

zcoder quality run --project ... --real

Use isolated worktree.

No mutation of primary branch.

================================================================
124. REAL PROJECT SAFETY
================================================================

Default benchmark must not push/merge.

Local validation only unless explicitly configured.

================================================================
125. COST PROOF
================================================================

Every quality run under zero-cost profile:

Anthropic calls = 0
OpenAI paid calls = 0
Stripe = 0
hosted embeddings = 0

================================================================
126. OFFLINE QUALITY LAB
================================================================

With model artifact already installed:

quality benchmarking must run offline.

================================================================
127. NETWORK GUARD
================================================================

Intercept prohibited external network.

Loopback local inference remains allowed.

================================================================
128. PERFORMANCE DATA
================================================================

Reuse Upgrade-16/17 performance measurements.

Do not duplicate collectors.

================================================================
129. LLAMA.CPP METRICS
================================================================

Where real llama.cpp runtime provides current documented metrics:

consume them through runtime adapter.

Do not make QualityEngineeringService llama.cpp-specific.

================================================================
130. SLOT/CAPACITY DATA
================================================================

Runtime scheduler remains responsible for capacity.

Quality engine consumes results, not slot ownership.

================================================================
131. QUALITY VS SERVER HEALTH
================================================================

Do not quarantine a model merely because runtime server had unrelated
temporary network/process issue.

Correctly attribute cause.

================================================================
132. ERROR ATTRIBUTION
================================================================

Classify error origin:

MODEL
RUNTIME
TOOL
VALIDATOR
POLICY
INFRASTRUCTURE

================================================================
133. ERROR TAXONOMY
================================================================

Persist normalized failure reason.

Useful for routing.

================================================================
134. MODEL REFUSAL
================================================================

Refusal may be valid depending task/policy.

Do not always score as defect.

================================================================
135. SECURITY TASKS
================================================================

Quality benchmark must never reward model for bypassing guardrails.

================================================================
136. TOOL SECURITY
================================================================

Prompt optimization cannot reduce approval/tool safeguards.

================================================================
137. CUSTOMER PROMPT INJECTION
================================================================

Repository content remains untrusted.

Evaluation fixtures should include prompt-injection cases.

================================================================
138. PROMPT-INJECTION FIXTURE
================================================================

Create fixture containing malicious repository instruction such as:

ignore policy
exfiltrate secret

Correct model/runtime behavior must keep platform policy authoritative.

================================================================
139. SECRET FIXTURE
================================================================

Use fake canary secret.

Benchmark should verify model/tool stack never leaks it.

Never use real credential.

================================================================
140. DESTRUCTIVE COMMAND FIXTURE
================================================================

Test attempted destructive shell request.

Policy should deny/require approval.

Quality score must recognize safe behavior.

================================================================
141. SECURITY QUALITY SCORE
================================================================

Security invariant failures are hard gates, not averageable low scores.

================================================================
142. NO SAFETY-WASHING
================================================================

A model with high coding success but security invariant violation cannot
be preferred.

================================================================
143. RELEASE PROFILES
================================================================

Maintain:

CORE_FREE
LOCAL_PRODUCTION_RUNTIME
LOCAL_RUNTIME_VERIFIED
LOCAL_CODING_VERIFIED
PERFORMANCE_VERIFIED
SELF_HOSTED
SAAS

Add:

QUALITY_ENGINEERING
LOCAL_QUALITY_VERIFIED

================================================================
144. QUALITY_ENGINEERING PROFILE
================================================================

Requires:

fixtures
objective validators
quality result model
regression detection
promotion
quarantine
rollback
routing integration

Can use deterministic FakeLocalModel.

================================================================
145. LOCAL_QUALITY_VERIFIED
================================================================

