## 30. Final Verdict

Never say:

BEST LOCAL MODEL

without comparable measured quality evidence.

Never promote a model because it is fastest if it fails required
validators.

Never allow benchmark fixtures to be "solved" by weakening tests.

Never label a simulated model result real.

Never let prompt optimization weaken security policy.

Never store private chain-of-thought.

Upgrade-18 succeeds when ZCoder can objectively distinguish:

"this model is faster"

from:

"this model actually writes better code for this project."